in @prism

in @optics
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens
in @mirror/lens/unix
in @mirror/store

# @mirror/lens/unix/fuse — kernel-mediated projection sub-species.
#
# The first concrete platform sub-species of @mirror/lens/unix (the
# family root at shards/mirror/lens/unix.mirror). Where the v0 floor
# discharges abstract bodies through `bootstrap/src/lens_unix.rs`'s
# materialize-to-tempdir `UnixLens` struct, this sub-species declares
# the kernel-mediated path: a FUSE filesystem reuses the
# fragmentation crate's existing fuser-backed implementation
# (vcs/git/src/fuse.rs, ~1012 lines, commit `f1e1135`) without
# materialization. Same shard content, same Unix surface, no copy.
#
# === Design lineage (2026-06-15) ===
#
# Four design questions closed by Alex + Reed this morning after sister
# Mara's FS-overlay survey identified fragmentation/vcs/git/src/fuse.rs
# as the load-bearing existing implementation:
#
#   1. Crate location: fragmentation-fuse workspace member. The FUSE
#      machinery is a substrate primitive (Apache-2.0 open side per
#      [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]); mirror consumes
#      it via this sub-species. Matches the
#      `docs/specs/mirror-native-vcs.md` §2.2 workspace plan.
#   2. Write semantics: read-only floor at v0. Read-only ships first;
#      the write path is MANDATORY for VM deployment and lands in v1
#      together with the @mirror/store Lens primitive (see roadmap
#      doc roadmap/wip/mirror-lens-unix.md).
#   3. Lifecycle: long-lived per-home FUSE mount. One mount per home
#      (~/.mirror, ~/.reed, ~/.mara); a supervision tree at each home
#      spawns on first need; cargo / erlc / flang invocations reuse
#      the same mount across calls. BEAM philosophy — long-lived
#      supervised processes, persistent state, not per-cargo-invocation
#      mount-then-unmount churn.
#   4. Lens primitive at @mirror/store altitude: deferred to v1; lands
#      together with write semantics. The two are a pair because write
#      through cross-shard references needs the Lens primitive at the
#      Splinter level; either alone is half a feature.
#
# === Body status ===
#
# Substrate-level declaration only this tick. The Rust extraction
# (lifting fragmentation/vcs/git/src/fuse.rs into a `fragmentation-fuse`
# workspace member with a `BackingStore` trait; introducing
# `SplinterBackingStore` consuming @mirror/store; swapping
# bootstrap/src/lens_unix.rs's `UnixLens` materialize-path to a
# kernel-mediated FUSE-backed path) is the NEXT tick. This shard
# paints the picture so the implementation tick has a target shape
# already declared at substrate altitude.
#
# v0 keeps the materialize sub-species as a fallback (declared as
# `@mirror/lens/unix/materialize` in a forward-promised sibling shard);
# this fuse sub-species becomes the default once the workspace extract
# lands. Read-only at v0 means `mount` and `path` and `backing` carry
# bodies; the family-root's `write` action declared in
# shards/mirror/lens/unix.mirror is forward-promised to v1 for this
# sub-species (the obligation block `\` stays empty at the family
# root, and the v1 cut lands write semantics + the
# @mirror/store Lens primitive together; see roadmap doc).
#
# === Substrate-pull placement ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/lens/unix/fuse.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/lens/unix/fuse` and only that. Sibling sub-species at
# `shards/mirror/lens/unix/<platform>.mirror` will declare the
# corresponding namespaces.
#
# Spec context: roadmap/wip/mirror-lens-unix.md (the v0+v1 cascade
#               this sub-species opens),
#               docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3, §5 (the ouroboros
#               pipeline; per-home gen_prism roots; the runtime-target
#               framing the family root closes),
#               docs/specs/mirror-native-vcs.md §2.2 (fragmentation
#               workspace layout this sub-species's Rust home rides on),
#               docs/specs/threat-model-v0.md §3 A4 (sign-verify at
#               spawn altitude; per-home FUSE mounts are the
#               spawn-isolation surface).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]]
#                      (the Rust home is fragmentation; mirror consumes
#                      the trait surface),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]
#                      (the open/closed contract — fragmentation-fuse
#                      is open; mirror consumes the open trait),
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (per-home
#                      supervision tree is the lifecycle altitude).
# Related shards: lens/unix.mirror (the family root; this sub-species's
#                 parent — abstract impedance surface declared there),
#                 lens.mirror (the family root above),
#                 store.mirror (the carrier; oid, bytes, shard_ref,
#                 splinter_graph — what the BackingStore trait abstracts
#                 over so the same fuser machinery serves
#                 SplinterBackingStore and GitBackingStore alike),
#                 glass.mirror (verdict / imperfect / transparency).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/lens/unix/fuse.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/lens/unix/fuse` and only that.

prism @mirror/lens/unix/fuse {
  focus mount
  project path
  split backing
  shift altitude
  settle mount
}

# === Backing store discriminator ===
#
# The substrate primitive the v0 → v1 extraction abstracts over.
# `vcs/git/src/fuse.rs` currently couples its fuser::Filesystem
# handler methods to a git repository; the extraction lifts that
# coupling behind a `BackingStore` trait so the same 26 handler
# methods, inode table, and transparent traversal serve any
# content-addressed store. The two concrete bindings at extract
# time:
#
#   splinter_backing — mirror's @mirror/store binding; consumes the
#                      Splinter / oid / shard_ref vocabulary; the
#                      canonical binding for v0 and beyond.
#   git_backing      — the existing fragmentation/vcs/git binding;
#                      kept as a sibling for adapter reuse and the
#                      cross-substrate cross-walk this sub-species
#                      preserves (per
#                      [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]]).
#
# Closed sum, no stringly tags per [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
type backing_store = splinter_backing | git_backing

# === Action surface ===
#
# Honest `partials` from birth per recognition #306: each action that
# can carry residual opacity returns `imperfect` from
# shards/glass.mirror. The family root at shards/mirror/lens/unix.mirror
# declares the parent surface (mount / path / read / write / stat); this
# sub-species's actions are the kernel-mediated specializations that
# refine the family root's abstract bodies. The names match by design
# so a downstream consumer can resolve at either altitude.

# mount(home) — bind a per-home FUSE mount at the home's canonical
# path (~/.mirror, ~/.reed, ~/.mara). Long-lived: one mount per home,
# spawned by the supervision tree at first need; survives cargo /
# erlc / flang invocations; drop semantics tied to home shutdown, not
# handle shutdown.
#
# `imperfect` because the mount can fail with opacity: the home's
# backing store may not be reachable (failure(reason)), the macFUSE /
# fuser kernel binding may be absent (partial(opacity) — kernel
# extension not loaded), or the mount-point may already be occupied
# by a stale mount (failure(reason)). On success, carries the FUSE
# mount handle.
mount(home: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# path(mount, p) — look up a Unix path within a mounted home view.
# Pure substrate at this sub-species's altitude: the fuser
# Filesystem's lookup / readdir handlers walk the backing store's
# oid-graph to resolve the path; this action declares that lookup
# without escaping the substrate.
#
# `imperfect` because the lookup can carry opacity: the path may not
# resolve in the mounted oid-graph (failure(reason)), the backing
# store may have drifted past verify (partial(opacity_map)), or the
# mount may have been unbound while the lookup was in flight
# (failure(reason)). On success, carries the resolved file handle.
path(mount: ref, p: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# backing(mount) — read the backing store discriminator for a mounted
# home view. Lets downstream consumers (Reflection reading
# cross-shard reference reports per error-as-question.md §5.3, the
# v1 Lens primitive composition) decide which carrier they're
# observing. Total at the substrate altitude — no opacity possible —
# so the return type is the closed-sum directly.
backing(mount: ref) -> backing_store { \ }

out @mirror/lens/unix/fuse
out backing_store
out mount
out path
out backing
